From d91e24b3f9ddda849539e7fd6b7c2ad77dfede4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:42:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The farm bubble bobs smoothly, as the partner's bubbles do

The meat bubble over the farmer moved its bob only once per game tick, so it went up and down in steps, while the
partner's status bubbles use the same bob between ticks (MOD_RENDER_ALPHA) and move smoothly. The farm bubble now
uses the partner's expression: the same path, speed and smoothness.
---
 src/main/bubble.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/bubble.c b/src/main/bubble.c
index dd2a1b15..789feab2 100644
--- a/src/main/bubble.c
+++ b/src/main/bubble.c
@@ -917,7 +917,8 @@ static int32_t ringAnyBubble(void)
  * twelve layouts (168-179) always talk through NPC slot 6, script 207's section 11; before the city grows, the File
  * City of a new game (204) has Tanemon in the same slot, and its section 11 keeps the same rule. The test here is: a day has passed since the last harvest (p31), or this is the first visit to Tanemon, who gives Meat
  * at once; Palmon and Vegiemon have no such first gift. A full stack keeps the bubble, as the harvest is still
- * there. Nothing is drawn while a script runs: the bubble would hang over the farmer's own dialogue.
+ * there. Nothing is drawn while a script runs: the bubble would hang over the farmer's own dialogue. It bobs as the
+ * partner's bubbles do, between the game's ticks too (MOD_RENDER_ALPHA), so it moves smoothly at 60 frames a second.
  */
 #define FARM_FIRST_SCREEN	168
 #define FARM_LAST_SCREEN	179
@@ -948,7 +949,7 @@ static void renderFarmBubble(void)
 	pos.vx = entity->posData->location.vx;
 	pos.vz = entity->posData->location.vz;
 	pos.vy = -DIGI_PARA(entity->type).height + 20 - 65 + entity->posData->location.vy +
-		 ((_sin((MOD_RING_CLOCK % 20) * 204) * 12) >> 12);
+		 ((_sin((((MOD_RING_CLOCK % 20) * 4096 + MOD_RENDER_ALPHA) * 512) / 81920) * 12) >> 12);
 	depth = worldPosToScreenPos(&pos, &screen);
 	if ((depth <= 0x200) || (depth >= 0x10000)) {
 		return;
-- 
2.55.0

